  <!-- #704: Faction/hero picker display characters (Kysaro's TAOM_FactionUI port). Each is read
       by id directly from the picker's C# service; none is a basic troop, none is in any
       notable_templates / taom_wanderers / party-template / upgrade list, so nothing ever spawns
       one in the world. occupation="NotAssigned" is the engine's own sentinel for "no spawner role"
       (TaleWorlds.CampaignSystem.Occupation): grepped against every TAOM Occupation.* usage in
       Main/ (CastleNotableMaintainer, TaomNotableSpawnModel, TaomPartyWageModel, LotrIssueService,
       the hero-commission/startup adapters) and none reads NotAssigned, Lord iterates only
       is_hero="true" heroes via Occupation.Lord checks, and vanilla's own notable/wanderer pools are
       explicit culture template lists (xml-data.md "Culture NPC Naming Convention"), not an
       enumeration of every NPCCharacter. is_hidden_encyclopedia keeps them off the Encyclopedia list
       too, mirroring characters/creature_bandits.xml's same-purpose "never normally visible" pattern.
       Each BodyProperties key is borrowed verbatim from an existing TAOM character of the same race
       and sex, named in its own comment; Kysaro re-tunes the face in the editor later. -->

